@SkryptX - it's actually already done the second way that you mentioned, via `pthread_setname_np()`. You just need `CONFIG_THREAD_NAME=y`.

See `lib/posix/pthread.c`.

From what I gather, `prctl()` is a linuxism. You could make a PR for it if you like, but I don't see any major advantage in adopting it (especially in the POSIX subsystem, given that it is non-portable / non-standard).

